<div class="bt-list"><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1">Categories</a> &gt; <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1174">topics</a> &gt; <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=101">biological and physical processes</a></div>
<div class="row">
<div class="this-term col-sm-12">
  <div class="pref-label">ocean processes</div>
  <div class="scope-note">Recurrent natural changes that are physical, biological, or chemical, actively affecting the seas and oceans.</div>
  <div class="non-pref">This category is also used with <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1034">sediment transport</a> for <span class="uf">marine sediment transport</span>,  with <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=531">hazards</a> for <span class="uf">ocean hazards</span>, and  with <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=810">ocean characteristics</a> for <span class="uf">oceans</span></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="row mb-4">
<div class="col-sm-12">
  <div class="col-sm-8"><b>Subtopics</b><br/><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=812" title="Movement of large masses of water within an ocean.">ocean circulation</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=814" title="Recurrent strong flows of seawater generated by wind or variations in water density along a given path.">ocean currents</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=822" title="A periodic movement of seawater caused by wind, tide, and currents.">ocean waves</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1168" title="The periodic rise and fall of the level of the sea due to the gravitational attraction of the moon and sun. Occurs twice each day.">tides (oceanic)</a><br/>
</div>
  <div class="col-sm-4"><b>See also</b><br/><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=707" title="Branch of earth sciences concerned with the physical processes of the oceans and continental margins.  We include here studies of large bodies of brackish and fresh water, such as lakes and rivers.">marine geophysics</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=2058" title="Decrease in the pH of ocean waters as a result of the increase in atmospheric carbon dioxide concentration.">ocean acidification</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=810" title="The attributes and process of seas and oceans.">ocean characteristics</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=818" title="Sciences involved in the study of geological, biological, chemical, and physical characteristics and processes of the oceans.">ocean sciences</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=823" title="Processes, including momentum, heat, gas and other exchanges, which result in profound effects on climate and interactions between the air in the lowest part of the atmosphere and the oceans.">ocean-atmosphere interaction</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1124" title="Open bodies of water, such as lakes, rivers, or streams.  All non-marine waters on the  surface of the earth, including fresh, brackish, and salt water.">surface water (non-marine)</a><br/>
</div>
</div>
</div>
